{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00705",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 2.82,
      "end_seconds": 16.32,
      "duration_seconds": 13.5,
      "text": "Good morning, doctor. I hope this isn't too trivial. My ears feel blocked, ever since I flew back from Boston on Friday."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 20.41,
      "end_seconds": 27.19,
      "duration_seconds": 6.78,
      "text": "Not trivial at all. Tell me what the blocked feeling is like."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 30.38,
      "end_seconds": 38.91,
      "duration_seconds": 8.53,
      "text": "Like I'm underwater. Muffled, and a sort of fullness, mostly in the right ear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 42.91,
      "end_seconds": 46.07,
      "duration_seconds": 3.16,
      "text": "When did it begin, exactly?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 49.2,
      "end_seconds": 59.72,
      "duration_seconds": 10.52,
      "text": "On the descent. They popped in the first ear, but the right one never did, and it's been four days now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 63.83,
      "end_seconds": 67.25,
      "duration_seconds": 3.42,
      "text": "Any pain in the ear? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 70.57,
      "end_seconds": 77.78,
      "duration_seconds": 7.21,
      "text": "A dull ache on the descent, but nothing since. Just the muffled feeling. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 80.83,
      "end_seconds": 85.86,
      "duration_seconds": 5.03,
      "text": "Does it crackle or pop when you swallow?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 88.74,
      "end_seconds": 94.01,
      "duration_seconds": 5.27,
      "text": "Occasionally, a little crackle. Then it goes quiet again."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 97.6,
      "end_seconds": 102.65,
      "duration_seconds": 5.05,
      "text": "Have you tried anything to clear it? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 105.92,
      "end_seconds": 114.02,
      "duration_seconds": 8.1,
      "text": "I tried holding my nose and blowing gently, a few times. I read it online. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 117.21,
      "end_seconds": 126.86,
      "duration_seconds": 9.65,
      "text": "That's a good method, as long as it's gentle. Let me look in your ear. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 144.18,
      "end_seconds": 146.08,
      "duration_seconds": 1.9,
      "text": "Of course."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 148.88,
      "end_seconds": 159.37,
      "duration_seconds": 10.49,
      "text": "The right eardrum is slightly pulled in, but it's intact and there's no fluid or infection that I can see."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 162.95,
      "end_seconds": 165.69,
      "duration_seconds": 2.74,
      "text": "Is it serious? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 169.0,
      "end_seconds": 181.24,
      "duration_seconds": 12.24,
      "text": "Not at all. It's a common thing after flying, when the tube that equalises pressure behind the eardrum is slow to open. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 184.65,
      "end_seconds": 188.64,
      "duration_seconds": 3.99,
      "text": "Will it clear by itself? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 192.23,
      "end_seconds": 197.03,
      "duration_seconds": 4.8,
      "text": "Almost always, within a week or two. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 199.98,
      "end_seconds": 203.89,
      "duration_seconds": 3.91,
      "text": "Is there anything I should do? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 207.41,
      "end_seconds": 217.14,
      "duration_seconds": 9.73,
      "text": "Chew gum or suck a sweet, yawn, and do that gentle blowing with your nose pinched, a few times a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 221.31,
      "end_seconds": 224.31,
      "duration_seconds": 3.0,
      "text": "I can do that. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 226.98,
      "end_seconds": 233.95,
      "duration_seconds": 6.97,
      "text": "Steam from a hot shower or a bowl of hot water also helps. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 237.64,
      "end_seconds": 240.94,
      "duration_seconds": 3.3,
      "text": "I'll do that tonight. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 244.33,
      "end_seconds": 255.02,
      "duration_seconds": 10.69,
      "text": "And don't fly again for now if you can avoid it, and don't put anything in the ear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 258.59,
      "end_seconds": 262.85,
      "duration_seconds": 4.26,
      "text": "Understood. What if it doesn't clear? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 266.28,
      "end_seconds": 276.4,
      "duration_seconds": 10.12,
      "text": "If it's not better in two weeks, or you get pain, discharge or dizziness, come back and see me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 279.15,
      "end_seconds": 283.57,
      "duration_seconds": 4.42,
      "text": "I will. Thank you so much. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 286.66,
      "end_seconds": 292.57,
      "duration_seconds": 5.91,
      "text": "You're welcome. Safe travels, whenever you next go. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 295.52,
      "end_seconds": 300.35,
      "duration_seconds": 4.83,
      "text": "Thank you, doctor. I'll chew plenty of gum. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 304.01,
      "end_seconds": 305.98,
      "duration_seconds": 1.97,
      "text": "Please do. ~"
    }
  ]
}
